  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PUBLIC PROCUREMENT REFORM IN NEPAL</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of the Grant is to help His Majestys Government of Nepal (HMGN) to enhance the quality of public procurement through procedural and institutional reforms, including adoption of a comprehensive procurement law, revision and consolidation of all existing procurement rules and regulations, preparation of a framework for institutionalizing procurement training, and implementation of training program. To meet this objective, the grant will help develop a draft modern transparent and competitive Public Procurement Law, and related rules and procedures.  In addition, it will help establish institutionalized training arrangements and conduct initial training program, particularly for trainers and officials responsible for the management of public procurement including contract administration.</narrative>
  </description>
